# CASM WP40 trusted reference: casmrelop1
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmrelop1 fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM. Proves the
# emitMaybeRecordHi/Lo hooks (WP40) do not change any program byte. One
# instance of each site from the WP40 plan's Dependency Review items 1-4
# recording under the *normal* (non-extraction) shape. Cross-check:
#   - brain/plans/2026-07-24-casm-phase8-wp40-relocation-table-and-emission-hooks.md
#
# WP41 -- updated with the R6 footer, the first real end-to-end proof that
# WP39's classification and WP40's recording produced the *correct*
# offsets, not merely that assembly didn't crash. Four relocation entries,
# in emission order: MID's ValHi (JMP, offset 2), LDA #>DATA's extracted
# ValLo (offset 4), .WORD DATA's ValHi (offset 8), .BYTE >DATA's extracted
# ValLo (offset 9). LDX #<DATA's ValLo (offset 6, low extraction) and
# .WORD DATA's ValLo (offset 7, the low half of a full value) are each
# correctly excluded. Cross-check:
#   - brain/plans/2026-07-25-casm-phase8-wp41-r6-footer-serialization.md
#
# Source (no .ORG):
#   - START: JMP MID
#   - MID: LDA #>DATA / LDX #<DATA / .WORD DATA / .BYTE >DATA
#   - DATA: NOP
#
# START = $3400 (no bytes). JMP MID is 3 bytes ($3400-$3402); MID = $3403.
# LDA #>DATA is 2 bytes ($3403-$3404, immediate, ValLo = DATA's high byte).
# LDX #<DATA is 2 bytes ($3405-$3406, immediate, ValLo = DATA's low byte --
# never relocatable). .WORD DATA is 2 bytes ($3407-$3408, little-endian
# full value). .BYTE >DATA is 1 byte ($3409, ValLo = DATA's high byte).
# DATA = $340A (immediately after), where NOP ($EA) is emitted. Program
# offsets (CasmPc - $3400): JMP's ValHi=2, LDA#'s ValLo=4, LDX#'s ValLo=6
# (excluded), .WORD's ValLo=7 (excluded)/ValHi=8, .BYTE's ValLo=9.
#
# Hand assembly:
#   00 34        PRG load-address header ($3400, little-endian)
#   4C 03 34     JMP $3403                    (MID)
#   A9 34        LDA #$34                     (DATA's high byte, $340A -> $34)
#   A2 0A        LDX #$0A                     (DATA's low byte, $340A -> $0A)
#   0A 34        .WORD $340A                  (little-endian: $0A, $34)
#   34           .BYTE $34                    (DATA's high byte again)
#   EA           NOP                          (at $340A, defines DATA)
#   02 00        R6 table entry: offset 2 (JMP's ValHi)
#   04 00        R6 table entry: offset 4 (LDA #>DATA's ValLo)
#   08 00        R6 table entry: offset 8 (.WORD's ValHi)
#   09 00        R6 table entry: offset 9 (.BYTE >DATA's ValLo)
#   00 34        R6 footer: base address ($3400, little-endian)
#   04 00        R6 footer: relocation entry count (4)
#   52 36        R6 footer: ASCII magic "R6"
#
# bytes: 27
# sha256: cc1a85db11b6ba1c441bc9bd1c0f8cf32cca0af292511ec0234516fd91922154

00 34
4C 03 34
A9 34
A2 0A
0A 34
34
EA
02 00
04 00
08 00
09 00
00 34
04 00
52 36
